 "content_notes": "Tone: absurd and ironic; the joke is on the fakes (a toupee sitting on a taped packet, cushion buttocks on swimming trunks, a cold latex bump), never on a person. Every case is a seizure by a named police force (Spain's National Police; Portugal's anti-narcotics police; Colombia's anti-narcotics police), a settled fact; the hook states the seizure. Everyone arrested is arrested or charged, not convicted, as far as reports show: never named, never given a face. The Barcelona passenger is drawn only from behind (the back of a generic head, no face) and as a dark silhouette; the Lisbon men and the Bogota passenger are dark rim-lit silhouettes (NOT A LIKENESS); 'police say' carries the allegation that the second Lisbon man was to receive the drugs. The Bogota passenger later said she felt trapped (2014 report); the reel does not judge her. Officers, the investigator and the inspector are generic figures in plain clothing with no badge, patch, flag, agency name or insignia; no weapon; no force shown; the pat-down is a gloved hand on a coat. Rooms, the checkpoint, the evidence table, the station and the departures area are illustrations, not reported scenes; no airline, airport sign or logo is copied. Every card is our own typed graphic; no dialogue or quotation card. Facts verified 2026-10-25.",
